{"claims":[{"claim_text":"The Democratic Socialists of America (DSA) does not claim to know exactly how a transition from capitalism to socialism will ultimately play out.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The Democratic Socialists of America (DSA) wants to build a socialist party that can take advantage of a crisis of legitimacy of capitalism when it arrives.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"A party can help foment a crisis by building powerful movements from below, including strikes, workplace takeovers, student occupations, and mass demonstrations, and by electing a socialist government.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Such mobilizations and a socialist government together would be able to create a rupture with the capitalist system.", "claim_types":["prediction"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"In a transitional period, a socialist government backed by popular mobilizations will have to do everything necessary to defend the mandate to carry out a program of redistribution, expropriation, and democratic reform of state institutions, since no ruling class has ever peacefully ceded power.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
